    r=[
      doc('I01','2026-06-02T08:00:00Z','SIGNED_INCIDENT_RULE','incident INC-72',{'ordering':'server sequence within signed incident ledger outranks client wall clock','closure':'requires business replay PASS','root_cause':'must be confirmed by signed causal analysis'},'The dashboard may receive delayed client messages whose displayed clocks are not authoritative. Within the signed incident ledger, increasing server sequence defines state transitions. Availability, drained queue, replay validation and incident closure are distinct. A hypothesis is not a confirmed root cause. The task requests a historical snapshot and does not authorize any remediation.'),
      doc('I04','2026-06-02T10:55:00Z','CLIENT_CHAT','INC-72 operator workstation',{'client_clock':'11:15','claim':'incident resolved'},'An operator typed that the incident was resolved after seeing an empty queue. The workstation clock is twenty minutes fast, and the message has no signed ledger sequence. It cannot supersede a signed validation failure. Its phrasing describes the operator’s assumption, not a tested business replay or a formal incident closure receipt.'),
      doc('I02','2026-06-02T10:10:00Z','SIGNED_INCIDENT_LEDGER','INC-72 sequence 401',{'sequence':401,'service_availability':'UNAVAILABLE','incident_status':'OPEN'},'The signed ledger first records a service outage. This is a historical transition, not necessarily the final snapshot. Later signed sequences may update specific state fields while leaving unrelated fields unchanged. Do not discard the incident identity when reading the queue monitor, which reports only its own subsystem and cannot close the incident.'),
      doc('I03','2026-06-02T10:35:00Z','SIGNED_INCIDENT_LEDGER','INC-72 sequence 402',{'sequence':402,'service_availability':'AVAILABLE','incident_status':'MONITORING'},'The service becomes available again and the formal incident moves to monitoring. The entry explicitly leaves business replay pending. No rollback was performed; restarting a client session is not a rollback of the deployed application. This record may establish availability but does not suffice to claim the business process is validated.'),
      doc('I05','2026-06-02T10:50:00Z','SIGNED_QUEUE_SNAPSHOT','INC-72 queue Q-A',{'queue_depth':0,'sample_complete':True},'Queue Q-A is empty at this complete snapshot. Empty work queues do not prove that messages were processed correctly, because rejected or dropped jobs also leave a queue. The number is nevertheless a valid queue-depth observation. It does not establish a causal analysis or an incident resolution state.'),
      doc('I06','2026-06-02T10:52:00Z','SIGNED_REPLAY_TEST','INC-72 replay RP-9',{'business_replay':'FAIL','failure':'missing acknowledgement on one committed item'},'The replay checks committed items against acknowledgements and fails on one missing acknowledgement. It is a functional business test, not a health probe. No later replay result is included before the cutoff. The failure remains authoritative despite the restored service and empty queue; the validation result must not be rewritten as NOT_RUN.'),
      doc('I07','2026-06-02T10:53:00Z','SIGNED_INCIDENT_LEDGER','INC-72 sequence 403',{'sequence':403,'incident_status':'OPEN','business_replay':'FAIL','rollback':'NOT_PERFORMED'},'Sequence 403 reopens the incident after the replay failure. It does not revoke the separately observed availability unless explicitly stated. The ledger confirms that no rollback occurred, differentiating monitoring actions from deployment transitions. An unsigned comment with a later displayed client time does not override this sequence.'),
      doc('I08','2026-06-02T10:54:00Z','UNCONFIRMED_HYPOTHESIS','INC-72 investigation',{'possible_cause':'cache eviction'},'The investigation proposes cache eviction as one possible cause and requests additional telemetry. There is no causal reproduction or signed confirmation. A specific hypothesis should not be presented as a confirmed root cause merely because it is the only hypothesis in the dossier. Preserve the distinction between an investigation lead and a conclusion.'),
      doc('I09','2026-06-02T10:56:00Z','SIGNED_COMPLETE_ANALYSIS_REGISTER','INC-72',{'confirmed_root_cause':None,'completed_causal_analyses':0},'The causal-analysis register is complete up to the cutoff and contains no completed confirmed analysis. This record supports null for the confirmed root cause. It does not imply that the incident has no physical cause or that all hypotheses are false. External knowledge about similar systems is not evidence for this specific incident.'),
      doc('I10','2026-06-02T10:58:00Z','SIGNED_CONSOLIDATED_REPORT','INC-72 as of cutoff',{'service_availability':'AVAILABLE','incident_status':'OPEN','business_replay':'FAIL','queue_depth':0,'rollback':'NOT_PERFORMED'},'The signed report consolidates the latest signed ledger state, replay and queue evidence. It certifies only the five fields listed, with independent meanings. It may replace their primary evidence but does not supply a confirmed root cause. It rejects the client chat as authority for closure because formal closure requires a passed replay.')]
